1
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:29,800
Can I borrow one of your men?

2
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:32,480
You want me to look after that woman?
I'm not doing it.

3
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:34,400
Anyway, I'm trusting you with my future.

4
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:37,040
Why do I have to do this?

5
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,520
So your work hours depend on me.

6
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,440
Since Man started boxing,

7
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:44,920
he's never lost to anyone. Except Arm.

8
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,120
Can we get back together?

9
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:54,920
From what I saw yesterday,
Oab seems to take good care of you too.

10
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:00,880
Dom!

11
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:09,080
<i>I never thought what I did</i>
<i>would make you uncomfortable.</i>

12
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:11,240
I still think we're the way we used to be.

13
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,520
Man is talented,

14
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:15,280
but he's lost before.

15
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:17,680
If he loses again,
it wouldn't be surprising.

16
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:20,960
KING BOXING CAMP

17
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,920
NARIS DAMRAT BRIDGE

18
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:24,640
You're not taking a break?

19
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:28,960
No. I don't want to lose to Man.

20
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:32,240
I've watched his fights a bunch of times.

21
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:34,680
We still have a shot at beating him.

22
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:49,040
You really think he can beat Man?

23
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:52,800
I think he can.

24
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:57,360
I told him to rest today, but he wouldn't.

25
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:01,920
That determination
is exactly what'll help him beat Man.

26
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:06,960
What about Mr. Phinit? What did he say?

27
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:09,640
He just asked for some details.

28
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:13,080
He asked for details this time?

29
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,680
- That's weird.
- He didn't.

30
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:18,360
His daughter did.

31
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:21,079
- Plern?
- Yeah.

32
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:24,320
She wanted to see the project herself, and

33
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:26,240
she asked to take Dom with her.

34
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:29,040
But he has a fight coming up.

35
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:33,840
If I say no, they won't give us the money.

36
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:36,560
Think he can handle it?

37
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:38,760
I don't know.

38
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,600
If we want their money,
we have to make a trade.

39
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:45,360
I think Plern is interested in Dom.

40
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:03,480
Fon.

41
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:05,640
Yes?

42
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:06,760
What's wrong?

43
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:08,360
You've been spacing out for a while.

44
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:14,440
Champ, can I take leave?

45
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:16,080
Leave for where?

46
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:36,840
- Got you.
- Whoa.

47
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:38,640
Dum!

48
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:39,960
Come on. Move.

49
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:42,760
- You took my pieces last turn.
- Come on.

50
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:44,360
Are they done training?

51
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:47,120
It's lunch break.
The fighters went to rest.

52
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:48,360
Are you here to see Oab?

53
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:50,440
Yes.

54
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,560
Fon.

55
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:54,440
Come on, move.

56
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:56,520
- Yeah.
- Why don't we talk inside?

57
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:06,040
- How should I move?
- Hey, Dom.

58
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:08,080
Going to see Plern?

59
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,360
Yes.

60
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:18,880
I'm moving. My turn.

61
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:22,240
That move, you're done.

62
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:27,040
I got distracted earlier. Hold on.

63
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,360
Go on. Can you take it?

64
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,480
Well…

65
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:41,920
I came to apologize about last night.

66
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:47,200
For avoiding me?

67
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:51,320
Yes.

68
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:06,080
I made you uncomfortable, didn't I?

69
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,480
Not at all.

70
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:14,800
I know you well, Fon.

71
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:19,240
You don't have to say that
just to make me feel better.

72
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:34,800
But…

73
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:44,240
Can I ask you to keep the ring
I gave you for now?

74
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:49,160
Maybe one day you might…

75
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:52,960
You might love me again.

76
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:05,200
Just stay like this with me
for a little while.

77
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,440
Pretend you still love me until…

78
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:16,280
Until what?

79
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:22,160
Until I can…

80
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:25,080
accept it.

81
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:29,200
Please.

82
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:37,880
It won't be long.

83
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:43,000
Just until the day Dom fights Man.

84
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:20,120
<i>Why does it have to be the day Dom fights?</i>
<i>What are you planning?</i>

85
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:22,800
To do what I should have done
a long time ago.

86
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:32,800
It's time karma caught up with him.

87
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:35,760
Boss Peng?

88
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:39,280
I stayed quiet and did nothing.

89
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:42,880
I let him hurt me as if I were
someone who couldn't fight back.

90
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,480
I've been waiting for the day I'm ready.

91
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:54,360
One chance. Just one.

92
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:56,840
And that one chance is the day Dom fights?

93
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:06,840
Either he goes down, or I do.

94
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:12,120
<i>If Dom fights,</i>

95
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:15,040
<i>he won't survive.</i>

96
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,640
You've been training for hours.

97
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:29,000
Where are you going with the bags?

98
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,840
Ratchaburi.

99
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:33,880
Ratchaburi?

100
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:35,840
I don't want to go to the beach anymore.

101
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:40,560
Either way, I can't go. I have to train.

102
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:41,640
What happened to your break?

103
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:44,280
- Back then I was tired, so--
- Go.

104
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:50,000
I said it because I was tired.
Once I've rested, I don't want to stop.

105
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:57,080
- I didn't bring any clothes.
- That's fine.

106
00:10:57,920 --> 00:10:59,840
If you don't have a change of clothes,
we'll buy some.

107
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:03,720
Can't we go another day? After my fight?

108
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:05,400
But I want to go today.

109
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:08,000
I know. But I'm not ready.

110
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:11,160
But are you ready in your heart?
If you are,

111
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:13,160
money can take care of the rest.

112
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:17,320
I'm not going.

113
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:27,240
Oab, the guy you assigned to me
doesn't do anything I ask.

114
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:29,880
And that fight he has to take,
how much is the prize money?

115
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,320
I'll pay it right now.

116
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:34,640
Then Dom won't have to fight or train.
He can come with me instead.

117
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:36,280
Plern, this isn't about money.

118
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:37,600
Then what is it?

119
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:39,640
Why are you taking this fight
so seriously?

120
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,880
Between the funding you need

121
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:44,480
and this fight,

122
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,320
which one matters more?

123
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:14,240
Fine. Let's go. If we're going, let's go.

124
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:17,320
Why are you agreeing now?

125
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,280
I'll get my things first.

126
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:31,160
Hey, after this,

127
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:34,080
can I ask you
not to take Dom out of town again?

128
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:37,400
You want him to stay and train?

129
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:44,760
Boxing is Dom's dream.

130
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:49,760
If he wants to fight on a big stage,
he has to be ready.

131
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:54,440
A boxer doesn't just want to step
into the ring.

132
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:56,880
He wants to win too.

133
00:12:58,160 --> 00:12:58,960
Okay.

134
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:03,440
Hey, Dom. What's going on?

135
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:05,280
I have to go out of town.

136
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,080
- With that client from the bar?
- Yeah.

137
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:12,320
Who is she?

138
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:14,320
Why does she seem so close with Oab?

139
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:17,160
Rich kid. Spoiled as hell.

140
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:20,440
I'm telling you, if her dad wasn't rich,

141
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:23,080
with that attitude,
she wouldn't have gotten this far.

142
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:28,280
I don't know
why Oab sent me to look after her.

143
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:30,080
But thanks for agreeing to do it.

144
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:31,120
Yeah.

145
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,360
I had no choice back there.

146
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:44,280
Between the money to build a new future

147
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:47,880
and getting revenge
on the person who killed my brother.

148
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:52,000
I could tell you were in a tough spot.

149
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:58,080
It's fine.
I'll only be out of town for one night.

150
00:13:58,160 --> 00:14:00,000
I'll be back training tomorrow.

151
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:38,360
Hey, we have to head back early tomorrow.

152
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:45,000
Have you ever been here before?

153
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:50,000
No. First time.

154
00:14:57,760 --> 00:15:00,120
I came here with my mom when I was little.

155
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:04,720
<i>We were ambushed.</i>

156
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:07,760
<i>My dad's men saved me.</i>

157
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:11,640
<i>But they couldn't save her.</i>

158
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,320
Plern!

159
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:25,800
Mom!

160
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:28,400
<i>I never trusted</i>
<i>my dad's bodyguards after that.</i>

161
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:32,240
<i>Because that day, I didn't see</i>
<i>a single one of them save my mom.</i>

162
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:37,400
If the memory is that painful,

163
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,320
why come back?

164
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,560
I wanted to see my mom.

165
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:52,680
I wanted to stand where she once stood.

166
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:56,160
Even after 20 years,

167
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:58,880
it still feels like
I'm standing right beside her.

168
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:13,400
Come on.
You came here to see your mom, not to cry.

169
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:16,720
Let her see

170
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:19,280
how happy you've become.

171
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:35,360
Dech's pretty good, Boss.

172
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:39,320
I've had him training
as Man's sparring partner for a while now.

173
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,000
He's improved a lot.

174
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:43,200
I'm thinking of pushing him after Man.

175
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:11,280
Dom didn't come.

176
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:15,839
I got what you wanted.

177
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:38,880
I heard you're having money problems.

178
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:42,240
There's a boxing camp
looking for fighters.

179
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,600
They'll pay you more

180
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:49,400
if you decide to move.

181
00:17:58,760 --> 00:18:00,880
Welcome to King Boxing Camp.

182
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:07,880
Oab.

183
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:15,120
You were waiting for me?

184
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:18,680
Yes.

185
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:40,200
How much do you trust me?

186
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:47,960
Enough to share
everything in my life with you.

187
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:54,560
Why do you ask?

188
00:18:56,600 --> 00:18:58,080
Have you changed your mind?

189
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:07,440
I want to know what your plan is

190
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:09,160
for the day of the fight.

191
00:19:32,800 --> 00:19:34,320
Hey, you.

192
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:37,960
There's only one bedroom,

193
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:39,600
so I'm just here to use the bathroom.

194
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:42,200
Can you sit and eat with me?

195
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:46,880
I'm not hungry. I have to wake up early,
so I'm going to sleep.

196
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:49,960
Can't you just sit with me while I eat?

197
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:58,960
Fine. But hurry. I need to sleep.

198
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:16,520
You're the only one
who dares to talk to me like this.

199
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:26,240
My dad's other men

200
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:27,640
just do whatever I tell them.

201
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:30,560
No one ever dares to go against me.

202
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:37,880
My job is to keep you safe. That's all.

203
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:40,080
I don't have to follow your orders.

204
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:45,440
Thank you.

205
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:52,240
You made today less sad
than I thought it would be.

206
00:21:15,840 --> 00:21:17,360
I should go to sleep.

207
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:19,840
Where are you going to sleep?

208
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:21,560
In the car.

209
00:21:22,560 --> 00:21:24,080
You can sleep on the sofa.

210
00:21:24,880 --> 00:21:26,200
No, it's fine.

211
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:28,200
I'm not going to do anything to you.

212
00:21:32,680 --> 00:21:34,040
I'll sleep in the car.

213
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:36,800
Make sure you lock up when you go inside.

214
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:49,000
Do you really think
everything will go according to plan?

215
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:52,000
It's possible
everything will go according to plan, Fon.

216
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:55,000
It's also possible that everything

217
00:21:56,360 --> 00:21:57,440
won't go according to plan.

218
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,240
Then can I have the police stand by?

219
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:06,200
Are you worried about me?

220
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:13,200
I just don't want anyone else
getting hurt.

221
00:22:15,520 --> 00:22:17,080
I thought you were worried about me.

222
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:29,000
It's okay, Fon.

223
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:32,800
I already have someone handling this.

224
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:36,440
The police?

225
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:44,920
Like I told Oab already.

226
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:47,440
I'll send some men
to cover different spots.

227
00:22:47,960 --> 00:22:49,320
That way, I can watch your backs.

228
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:53,160
Thanks, man. Are you sure
you won't get yourself in trouble?

229
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:58,160
I think a match
involving an influential camp

230
00:22:58,680 --> 00:22:59,760
should be enough to request support.

231
00:23:05,320 --> 00:23:07,680
Hey. Your car keys.

232
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:09,600
Come inside first.

233
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:11,000
No. I'm going to train.

234
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:21,400
Get in the car.

235
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,360
Stay home. It's safer.

236
00:23:29,920 --> 00:23:31,600
Get in. I'll drive you there.

237
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:38,280
Hey.

238
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:40,000
Don't make this difficult.

239
00:23:40,080 --> 00:23:42,200
Taking a taxi or riding with me
is the same thing.

240
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:44,000
How is it the same?

241
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:45,800
Either way, we'll get to the camp.

242
00:23:45,880 --> 00:23:46,840
Go, get in.

243
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:51,800
If you don't,

244
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:53,760
I'll just follow you there anyway.

245
00:23:54,880 --> 00:23:57,640
And if Oab sees you let me drive alone,

246
00:23:57,720 --> 00:24:00,880
he'll blame you
for not doing your job properly.

247
00:24:25,360 --> 00:24:26,840
You're not going to work today?

248
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:29,520
I took the day off.

249
00:24:30,480 --> 00:24:32,760
I'm in the narcotics unit,

250
00:24:32,840 --> 00:24:35,160
but I barely get to arrest anyone.

251
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:38,080
They probably have a lot of connections.

252
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:41,960
The more powerful they get,
the more connections they have.

253
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:45,080
One day, you'll have to choose a side.

254
00:24:47,440 --> 00:24:50,600
But you're not ordinary either.
You must have connections too.

255
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:51,720
Right?

256
00:24:52,280 --> 00:24:53,520
Trying to get information out of me?

257
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:02,280
Hey. People don't ask things like this.

258
00:25:09,320 --> 00:25:10,240
You understand?

259
00:25:19,600 --> 00:25:21,160
But if I know who they are,

260
00:25:21,240 --> 00:25:23,000
I can be more careful.

261
00:25:23,600 --> 00:25:25,480
You need to be careful with everyone.

262
00:25:28,840 --> 00:25:30,800
I'm the only one
you don't have to worry about.

263
00:25:42,920 --> 00:25:44,000
Okay.

264
00:25:45,200 --> 00:25:47,600
So you didn't get any information, huh?

265
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:52,800
Since you're free today,
spend the day with me.

266
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:00,680
Okay.

267
00:26:00,760 --> 00:26:01,560
‪Perfect.

268
00:26:06,560 --> 00:26:10,000
- Make it clean. You're such a slacker.
- Yes.

269
00:26:14,680 --> 00:26:16,160
- Dum.
- What?

270
00:26:16,240 --> 00:26:17,280
Look.

271
00:26:18,920 --> 00:26:21,800
Hey. The rich kid's here.

272
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:23,280
Dum.

273
00:26:23,360 --> 00:26:25,880
If I had a rich girl
chasing after me like Dom has,

274
00:26:25,960 --> 00:26:28,600
I wouldn't want anything else.
I'd just stay home and enjoy the money.

275
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:30,720
- Really?
- Call me a gold digger, I don't care.

276
00:26:31,480 --> 00:26:33,080
- Seriously.
- Come on.

277
00:26:33,160 --> 00:26:36,120
The people who judge us
don't struggle like we do.

278
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:37,520
Let them talk.

279
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:39,720
- You're funny.
- Huh?

280
00:26:40,360 --> 00:26:41,720
Don't you think the same?

281
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:42,800
I don't know.

282
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:49,160
Hey, here he comes.

283
00:26:49,240 --> 00:26:51,040
The rich man's son-in-law is here!

284
00:26:51,120 --> 00:26:52,200
Your rich man's ass.

285
00:26:52,960 --> 00:26:53,880
Hey.

286
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:56,720
If my dad were rich,
I wouldn't be mopping floors here.

287
00:26:57,840 --> 00:26:58,760
Plern.

288
00:27:02,920 --> 00:27:03,920
Plern?

289
00:27:04,760 --> 00:27:06,320
You came to watch Dom train?

290
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:08,000
Yes.

291
00:27:08,080 --> 00:27:12,400
Usually Dom takes care of me.
So today, I thought I'd take care of him.

292
00:27:13,160 --> 00:27:14,080
Hey.

293
00:27:17,920 --> 00:27:19,040
- Hey.
- Oab.

294
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:22,480
Good.

295
00:27:22,560 --> 00:27:24,640
Dom, your new sparring partner is here.

296
00:27:25,680 --> 00:27:28,760
For the next seven days,
you'll only spar with Dech.

297
00:27:30,680 --> 00:27:32,240
Why change my sparring partner?

298
00:27:32,320 --> 00:27:34,600
Until now,
Dech was Man's sparring partner.

299
00:27:35,960 --> 00:27:37,200
They're about the same level.

300
00:27:38,040 --> 00:27:42,440
If you can beat Dech,
you might be able to beat Man.

301
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:47,240
Dum, take Dech to change.

302
00:27:47,320 --> 00:27:49,360
I'll take him. Then we can start training.

303
00:27:50,800 --> 00:27:52,480
- Come on.
- Yes, Dum.

304
00:28:40,840 --> 00:28:42,080
What are you thinking about, Fon?

305
00:28:48,320 --> 00:28:49,360
Nothing.

306
00:28:51,320 --> 00:28:52,560
But your face gives you away.

307
00:28:56,680 --> 00:28:57,840
Oab.

308
00:28:57,920 --> 00:28:58,880
Yes?

309
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:02,080
Who is the woman with Dom?

310
00:29:02,760 --> 00:29:04,240
I've never seen her before.

311
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:07,040
Changing the subject, aren't you?

312
00:29:11,480 --> 00:29:14,240
Fine. If I answer, will you tell me

313
00:29:14,320 --> 00:29:16,360
what you were
really thinking about just now?

314
00:29:22,640 --> 00:29:23,480
Yes.

315
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:28,720
Plern is my investor's daughter.

316
00:29:31,920 --> 00:29:34,400
But it looks like she really likes Dom.

317
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:45,960
Now, will you tell me
what you were thinking about?

318
00:29:55,320 --> 00:29:56,240
Well…

319
00:29:56,760 --> 00:29:58,720
I'm just worried about you.

320
00:29:59,680 --> 00:30:02,000
The fight is getting closer.

321
00:30:02,080 --> 00:30:04,000
From what I've heard about your plan,

322
00:30:04,520 --> 00:30:07,240
it's no different from walking in there
to get yourself killed.

323
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:17,080
Fon, don't worry.

324
00:30:19,520 --> 00:30:21,160
I'll come back to you.

325
00:30:35,400 --> 00:30:38,480
I should get back to work.

326
00:30:40,280 --> 00:30:41,200
Okay.

327
00:31:09,240 --> 00:31:11,160
What's wrong with you?

328
00:31:11,240 --> 00:31:13,200
Get up and talk to me.

329
00:31:18,240 --> 00:31:19,760
What am I supposed to do about Plern?

330
00:31:22,800 --> 00:31:24,480
Just marry her

331
00:31:24,560 --> 00:31:26,560
and bring me along.

332
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:31,080
It's better for you.
You can finally stay away from Fon.

333
00:31:31,960 --> 00:31:34,240
You know you shouldn't mess
with your boss's woman.

334
00:31:34,320 --> 00:31:36,160
Yeah, I know.

335
00:31:36,760 --> 00:31:38,800
Yeah, then that's it.

336
00:31:42,600 --> 00:31:45,240
See? This is you.

337
00:31:45,320 --> 00:31:47,880
The moment I say something
you don't like, you walk away.

338
00:31:47,960 --> 00:31:50,080
Fine, I'll get some sleep.

339
00:32:26,720 --> 00:32:27,680
Coffee.

340
00:32:31,200 --> 00:32:32,800
You're here late.

341
00:32:35,880 --> 00:32:37,600
Did you talk to Dech?

342
00:32:41,360 --> 00:32:42,320
Yeah.

343
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:48,000
He said you might not win.

344
00:32:50,120 --> 00:32:51,560
And you're not worried?

345
00:32:53,280 --> 00:32:54,760
I want you to win.

346
00:32:56,640 --> 00:32:58,880
But that day, Man isn't my target.

347
00:33:10,600 --> 00:33:13,120
Tomorrow, I'm going to watch you
train with Dech.

348
00:33:15,240 --> 00:33:18,080
I want to see
what it'll take for you to beat Man.

349
00:33:23,200 --> 00:33:24,160
But before that,

350
00:33:24,240 --> 00:33:26,120
you have to beat me first.

351
00:34:39,159 --> 00:34:40,280
When did he leave?

352
00:34:40,880 --> 00:34:42,239
He didn't show up for training,

353
00:34:42,320 --> 00:34:45,080
so I checked his room.
He'd already packed everything and left.

354
00:34:45,159 --> 00:34:46,360
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

355
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:51,000
I sent people to look for him.

356
00:34:51,080 --> 00:34:53,400
I was going to tell you
as soon as we found out.

357
00:34:53,480 --> 00:34:55,239
So? Did you find him?

358
00:34:55,320 --> 00:34:56,920
- Huh?
- Yes, Boss.

359
00:34:57,000 --> 00:34:57,960
We found him.

360
00:35:20,920 --> 00:35:21,880
Hello.

361
00:35:26,320 --> 00:35:27,400
Oab!

362
00:35:30,080 --> 00:35:31,320
Peng and his men are at the boxing camp.

363
00:35:31,400 --> 00:35:33,000
Stay here and wait for me.

364
00:35:36,360 --> 00:35:37,720
I'll come see you tomorrow.

365
00:35:43,640 --> 00:35:44,440
Where is he?

366
00:35:48,240 --> 00:35:49,440
Bring my man here.

367
00:35:50,600 --> 00:35:53,080
Your man is with you.

368
00:35:53,160 --> 00:35:54,240
Why would he be here?

369
00:35:54,320 --> 00:35:56,160
Search until we find Dech!

370
00:35:57,120 --> 00:35:58,200
- Hey!
- Hey!

371
00:35:58,280 --> 00:35:59,920
What's the problem?

372
00:36:00,680 --> 00:36:01,840
Come on!

373
00:36:02,400 --> 00:36:04,480
You're searching my place?

374
00:36:04,560 --> 00:36:06,400
Then you'll have to go through me.

375
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:13,200
Take this!

376
00:36:15,480 --> 00:36:17,800
You dare come here.
You're not afraid of dying?

377
00:36:22,320 --> 00:36:23,600
Do you want to settle this?

378
00:36:26,440 --> 00:36:28,720
If I was afraid, I wouldn't be here.

379
00:36:33,360 --> 00:36:35,640
My men told me you bought Dech.

380
00:36:36,600 --> 00:36:37,560
That's right.

381
00:36:40,160 --> 00:36:42,040
You disrespected me.

382
00:36:43,640 --> 00:36:45,000
Because you deserved it.

383
00:36:54,640 --> 00:36:55,920
Is it you?

384
00:36:56,560 --> 00:36:57,920
The temple fair boxer

385
00:36:58,880 --> 00:37:00,280
who's going to fight Man.

386
00:37:03,560 --> 00:37:06,120
Get out of my place.

387
00:37:37,280 --> 00:37:40,200
I'll leave when I get my man back.

388
00:37:58,440 --> 00:38:01,200
You'll get your man back
if he chooses to go with you.

389
00:38:35,280 --> 00:38:36,360
I'm sorry, Boss.

390
00:38:50,800 --> 00:38:52,200
Are you sure, Dech?

391
00:38:53,400 --> 00:38:55,120
Save your voice for cheering at the fight.

392
00:39:12,240 --> 00:39:15,240
I knew it. I knew he'd come.

393
00:39:15,840 --> 00:39:17,240
I was right to have you stay here.

394
00:39:18,760 --> 00:39:20,440
Otherwise, you'd be dead already.

395
00:39:23,160 --> 00:39:24,200
Hey.

396
00:39:25,040 --> 00:39:27,160
Don't think
Peng will give you another chance.

397
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:31,080
If you go back, he'll kill you.

398
00:39:32,800 --> 00:39:36,520
But if you stay here,
I'll guarantee your safety.

399
00:39:39,920 --> 00:39:40,920
- Yes, Boss.
- Good.

400
00:39:41,640 --> 00:39:43,400
Just don't go anywhere alone.

401
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:47,760
I'm going to bed. Early training tomorrow.

402
00:39:47,840 --> 00:39:48,960
Wait.

403
00:39:50,840 --> 00:39:51,960
Stay and talk with me.

404
00:39:56,760 --> 00:39:58,600
- Come on, Dech.
- I'll head out.

405
00:39:58,680 --> 00:39:59,680
Don't stress.

406
00:40:12,720 --> 00:40:14,560
<i>You're too slow.</i>

407
00:40:21,560 --> 00:40:22,800
<i>Throw your punches faster.</i>

408
00:40:24,480 --> 00:40:25,440
<i>Dodge faster.</i>

409
00:40:27,600 --> 00:40:30,720
<i>If you can speed up,</i>
<i>you'll have a chance of beating him.</i>

410
00:40:45,920 --> 00:40:47,440
Are you taking me to work today?

411
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:50,560
Can I have one day with you?

412
00:40:53,240 --> 00:40:54,520
But I just took a day off.

413
00:40:54,600 --> 00:40:57,280
- If I take another day--
- I'm only asking for today.

414
00:40:57,360 --> 00:40:58,720
I mean it.

415
00:41:00,800 --> 00:41:02,760
The day is coming soon.

416
00:41:03,760 --> 00:41:06,600
After that day, I don't know
if I'll have days like this again.

417
00:41:54,600 --> 00:41:56,600
Excuse me, what time is it?

418
00:41:57,880 --> 00:41:59,120
It's 8:40 a.m.

419
00:41:59,800 --> 00:42:00,800
Thanks.

420
00:42:09,000 --> 00:42:09,920
Going to see Plern?

421
00:42:32,440 --> 00:42:33,720
Wow, you're early.

422
00:42:33,800 --> 00:42:35,160
Can I quit?

423
00:42:37,120 --> 00:42:39,680
Can I stop being your bodyguard?

424
00:42:41,600 --> 00:42:42,720
No.

425
00:42:57,680 --> 00:42:59,800
If you can't tell me why, you can't quit.

426
00:43:01,240 --> 00:43:03,000
Go back to camp and train.

427
00:43:04,920 --> 00:43:07,480
I think
you should focus on your fight first.

428
00:43:08,000 --> 00:43:09,440
It's only a few days away.

429
00:43:11,720 --> 00:43:13,680
After the fight, we'll talk.

430
00:43:31,520 --> 00:43:32,960
Why?

431
00:43:34,000 --> 00:43:37,120
Is being with me really that hard for you?

432
00:43:44,240 --> 00:43:45,480
Is this your house?

433
00:43:50,120 --> 00:43:51,920
I built this house

434
00:43:52,960 --> 00:43:56,560
with the money I saved from construction.

435
00:44:10,520 --> 00:44:11,960
Everything I do now

436
00:44:12,600 --> 00:44:15,080
is because I want to have enough money
to come back to you.

437
00:44:18,640 --> 00:44:20,280
When we get married,

438
00:44:23,680 --> 00:44:25,120
I want you to live comfortably.

439
00:44:26,440 --> 00:44:28,040
I don't want you
worrying about money anymore.

440
00:44:30,480 --> 00:44:32,320
I want us to spend our time together,

441
00:44:35,360 --> 00:44:36,840
have a warm family,

442
00:44:39,480 --> 00:44:43,160
become a father,
teach my child how to ride a bike,

443
00:44:44,880 --> 00:44:47,000
and spend my life here with you.

444
00:45:12,040 --> 00:45:14,800
If I don't get the chance
to spend my life here with you,

445
00:45:19,320 --> 00:45:20,280
at least

446
00:45:22,000 --> 00:45:24,560
I want everything I've worked for

447
00:45:26,880 --> 00:45:28,480
to go to the person I want it to.

448
00:45:31,880 --> 00:45:34,120
GOVERNMENT SAVINGS BANK

449
00:45:40,160 --> 00:45:41,120
Oab.

450
00:45:43,280 --> 00:45:44,840
Can you change your mind?

451
00:45:48,840 --> 00:45:51,120
Your plan is like walking to your death.

452
00:45:52,400 --> 00:45:54,920
- There has to be a better way.
- Fon.

453
00:46:01,160 --> 00:46:02,560
I'm sorry, Fon.

454
00:46:11,640 --> 00:46:12,560
Oab.

455
00:46:14,400 --> 00:46:16,520
Arm is already dead.

456
00:46:17,320 --> 00:46:20,920
Whether Peng lives or dies
won't change anything.

457
00:46:23,400 --> 00:46:24,960
But if you die…

458
00:46:27,880 --> 00:46:29,200
You'll be hurt?

459
00:46:40,560 --> 00:46:41,880
If you die,

460
00:46:42,720 --> 00:46:45,160
how many of your men
will suffer because of it?

461
00:46:55,200 --> 00:46:56,800
I've signed a transfer document for you.

462
00:47:00,720 --> 00:47:01,880
Oab.

463
00:47:02,880 --> 00:47:03,840
Fon.

464
00:47:06,960 --> 00:47:08,400
Don't ask me for what I can't give.

465
00:47:10,400 --> 00:47:14,160
I'm not doing this
just because of the person we lost.

466
00:47:14,240 --> 00:47:16,080
If Peng is still alive,

467
00:47:16,960 --> 00:47:19,960
he'll never let me or the people I love

468
00:47:20,480 --> 00:47:22,480
live in peace.

469
00:47:39,720 --> 00:47:40,960
Fight!

470
00:47:41,040 --> 00:47:42,640
- Hey, don't rush.
- Dom!

471
00:47:43,200 --> 00:47:44,240
Watch first.

472
00:47:44,320 --> 00:47:45,600
You'll get hit.

473
00:47:45,680 --> 00:47:46,880
Hey, nice.

474
00:47:58,120 --> 00:47:59,240
Back up!

475
00:48:05,640 --> 00:48:07,360
Good. Stick to his game.

476
00:48:07,440 --> 00:48:10,120
- Guard! Good!
- Dom, stay sharp!

477
00:48:10,720 --> 00:48:12,280
Dom, don't slip up!

478
00:48:14,520 --> 00:48:16,040
- Come on!
- Go for it!

479
00:48:16,120 --> 00:48:18,000
- Guard!
- Dom!

480
00:48:19,240 --> 00:48:21,320
To your corners!

481
00:48:22,320 --> 00:48:24,080
Dum, get the chair.

482
00:48:26,520 --> 00:48:27,440
Dom, come on.

483
00:48:28,800 --> 00:48:30,320
Hey, Dom. What's wrong with you?

484
00:48:30,400 --> 00:48:31,600
Focus!

485
00:48:31,680 --> 00:48:32,800
This isn't like you.

486
00:48:32,880 --> 00:48:34,720
You can do better than this.

487
00:48:37,200 --> 00:48:38,120
Water.

488
00:48:40,000 --> 00:48:41,120
Come on.

489
00:48:45,960 --> 00:48:47,000
Go, fight!

490
00:48:48,680 --> 00:48:49,520
Go for it!

491
00:48:49,600 --> 00:48:51,600
NO GAMBLING

492
00:48:51,680 --> 00:48:52,880
Go!

493
00:48:53,760 --> 00:48:54,960
- Come on!
- Stay calm.

494
00:48:55,040 --> 00:48:57,040
Good. Keep your guard up.

495
00:48:57,640 --> 00:49:00,680
Yeah, that's it. Back up first.

496
00:49:00,760 --> 00:49:02,440
- Take it easy.
- Go!

497
00:49:02,520 --> 00:49:05,400
- Block! Yeah!
- Guard up!

498
00:49:05,480 --> 00:49:06,600
Hey!

499
00:49:06,680 --> 00:49:07,840
Don't drop your guard.

500
00:49:11,800 --> 00:49:13,120
Yes!

501
00:49:21,760 --> 00:49:24,320
If you can move like this,
you'll definitely beat him, Dom.

502
00:49:24,400 --> 00:49:26,440
Has Man gotten slower?

503
00:49:27,120 --> 00:49:28,000
He's on drugs.

504
00:49:29,600 --> 00:49:31,080
No matter how fast he is,

505
00:49:31,680 --> 00:49:34,480
the drugs will slow down his reflexes.

506
00:49:34,560 --> 00:49:36,160
But even slowed down,

507
00:49:36,240 --> 00:49:38,680
he's still a great boxer.

508
00:49:39,960 --> 00:49:43,160
He's got power, he's smart,
and he wants to win.

509
00:49:44,560 --> 00:49:45,480
Dech.

510
00:49:45,560 --> 00:49:49,080
Dech, your mom's calling.
You gonna answer or call her back?

511
00:49:49,160 --> 00:49:50,920
Yeah, answer it. I'll be right there.

512
00:49:53,320 --> 00:49:55,080
You're no different from Man.

513
00:49:55,160 --> 00:49:59,160
It comes down
to who wants to win more, you or him.

514
00:50:07,040 --> 00:50:08,520
I have to win.

515
00:50:14,720 --> 00:50:15,680
Really, Mom?

516
00:50:18,080 --> 00:50:19,040
Hurry up.

517
00:50:19,120 --> 00:50:21,760
- This client is always on time.
- Got it.

518
00:50:21,840 --> 00:50:22,840
- We can't be late.
- Dum.

519
00:50:22,920 --> 00:50:24,800
Can I go see my mom?

520
00:50:24,880 --> 00:50:26,600
How can you go?

521
00:50:26,680 --> 00:50:28,000
Peng's already after you.

522
00:50:28,600 --> 00:50:29,760
But I really have to go.

523
00:50:33,880 --> 00:50:34,800
Pong.

524
00:50:35,760 --> 00:50:37,280
Dech wants to go out.

525
00:50:37,360 --> 00:50:38,880
I have something to do at the casino.

526
00:50:39,480 --> 00:50:41,680
- Can you wait for me a bit?
- I have to go now.

527
00:50:43,360 --> 00:50:46,400
Then you and Haw should go with him.

528
00:50:46,480 --> 00:50:47,800
I can't.

529
00:50:47,880 --> 00:50:49,920
I have a client
coming to pick up liquor at the bar.

530
00:50:50,000 --> 00:50:52,200
Haw and I need to prepare everything.

531
00:50:52,280 --> 00:50:53,280
We can't go right now.

532
00:50:55,320 --> 00:50:56,440
Then I'll go with him.

533
00:50:56,520 --> 00:50:57,480
Are you crazy?

534
00:50:58,240 --> 00:51:00,400
One of you is about to fight Peng's man,

535
00:51:00,480 --> 00:51:02,680
and the other just betrayed him.

536
00:51:02,760 --> 00:51:04,840
If you two go together, you're both dead.

537
00:51:05,600 --> 00:51:07,240
It's better than letting him go alone.

538
00:51:08,360 --> 00:51:10,960
He'll go anyway.
Even if we try to stop him,

539
00:51:11,040 --> 00:51:13,120
you can tell he won't listen.

540
00:51:15,480 --> 00:51:18,440
You're right. It's still the safer option.

541
00:51:22,320 --> 00:51:23,840
Should I go with them too?

542
00:51:24,520 --> 00:51:25,520
No, you don't have to.

543
00:51:25,600 --> 00:51:27,680
You're just slacking off
to avoid carrying stuff.

544
00:51:27,760 --> 00:51:29,400
No, Dum.

545
00:51:29,480 --> 00:51:31,640
Three people are better than two, right?

546
00:51:38,000 --> 00:51:41,000
Up to Pong.
If he's okay with it, I'm okay.

547
00:51:44,560 --> 00:51:46,200
Go, but come straight back.

548
00:51:47,400 --> 00:51:48,240
Yes.

549
00:51:51,200 --> 00:51:54,200
Dom, is this around Plern's place
where you work?

550
00:51:57,720 --> 00:51:58,560
What kind of work does she do?

551
00:52:00,680 --> 00:52:02,320
Pay those people back quickly, Mom.

552
00:52:02,960 --> 00:52:04,280
Don't borrow from them again.

553
00:52:04,360 --> 00:52:05,400
Okay.

554
00:52:07,200 --> 00:52:11,120
Anyone who betrays me dies.

555
00:52:12,720 --> 00:52:14,440
If they die today,

556
00:52:16,600 --> 00:52:17,840
this fight means nothing, right?

557
00:52:18,520 --> 00:52:20,080
The boxer won't fight,

558
00:52:20,160 --> 00:52:22,200
and the camp owner will be dead.

559
00:52:29,640 --> 00:52:31,920
You rushed here
because your mom needed money?

560
00:52:32,000 --> 00:52:33,600
She borrowed from loan sharks.

561
00:52:33,680 --> 00:52:34,640
Why?

562
00:52:35,560 --> 00:52:38,680
My mom gambles.
She goes to the gambling den after work.

563
00:52:39,800 --> 00:52:41,400
I've paid off her debt so many times.

564
00:52:43,320 --> 00:52:44,680
But it never ends.

565
00:52:45,200 --> 00:52:48,560
So you risked switching camps
to get money for your mom?

566
00:52:48,640 --> 00:52:52,320
You're right, Dom.
They came to collect yesterday.

567
00:52:52,400 --> 00:52:54,480
They said if she didn't pay them back
by tonight,

568
00:52:54,560 --> 00:52:58,640
they'd beat her up.
That's why my mom called me for money.

569
00:53:11,800 --> 00:53:12,840
Are you full?

570
00:53:47,280 --> 00:53:49,800
Wait here for a moment, Fon.
I'll be right back.

571
00:53:49,880 --> 00:53:50,800
Is something wrong?

572
00:53:52,000 --> 00:53:54,520
I'm going to the bathroom. Just wait here.

573
00:54:28,240 --> 00:54:29,320
Something's going on, right?

574
00:54:31,920 --> 00:54:33,200
Get down.

575
00:54:34,360 --> 00:54:37,040
You said bathroom, but went the other way.

576
00:54:40,320 --> 00:54:41,640
Stay here and wait for me.

577
00:54:47,000 --> 00:54:49,000
Six against one? That won't work.

578
00:54:58,760 --> 00:55:00,120
It's only six people.

579
00:55:01,800 --> 00:55:02,920
Trust me.

580
00:56:35,280 --> 00:56:36,880
Who was the person who died?

581
00:56:40,880 --> 00:56:42,440
Have you been with Oab for a long time?

582
00:56:42,520 --> 00:56:44,680
What about you, Plern?
How long have you been with Dom?

583
00:56:48,040 --> 00:56:49,040
For a while now.

584
00:56:50,800 --> 00:56:52,280
If I don't come back this time,

585
00:56:52,360 --> 00:56:53,880
take all the money I gave you

586
00:56:53,960 --> 00:56:57,120
and run as far away as you can.
Understand?

587
00:56:57,200 --> 00:56:59,680
You weren't really working
in road construction, were you?

588
00:57:01,480 --> 00:57:02,240
This way, Boss.

589
00:57:03,080 --> 00:57:04,440
Hello, Boss.

590
00:57:05,240 --> 00:57:07,160
Hey, man. Long time no see.

591
00:57:09,320 --> 00:57:11,560
A job that sent you two
out of town together?

592
00:57:12,160 --> 00:57:15,560
And now this too.
How did you make her think you're dating?

593
00:57:54,840 --> 00:58:00,720
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
